{"type": "matching", "introText": "<p>5-6 Ascending Sequence</p>

<p>Another common ascending scale pattern of the 17th and 18th centuries is the 5-6 sequence &ndash; in which the voice that begins on 5 moves to 6 before the bass ascends. Practice this pattern in a variety of scales.</p>

